    "explanation": "The four HDF5 datasets represent independently partitioned permutations of the underlying 90,950 uTHCD samples. Sample hash analysis demonstrates that images in the Test partition of the 80/20, 85/15, and 90/10 splits partially overlap with the Training partition of the 70/30 split, and vice versa. Evaluating the ensemble on any single split's test set without accounting for this overlap causes data leakage for the models that included those samples during training. Consequently, a strictly leak-free ensemble evaluation requires a globally disjoint test set: samples never seen in the training sets of ANY of the 4 models."
